  "notes": [
    "v_rate_bps = result.victim.completed_bytes / (p4m.hardware_window_ns / 1e9) = bytes/(ns/1e9), not bytes/ns (16 MiB for the formal60 shape)",
    "a_window_rate_bps is the A completion rate inside the P4M observer window; not AXI/bus throughput",
    "a_whole_hpm_active_cycles = result.aggressor.active_cycles (whole run, separate from the observer window)",
    "whole-run HPM counters for both sides: result.victim.* and result.aggressor.* (iotlb_miss, s1_ptw, s2_ptw)",
    "startup_domain is the software irq-pair domain; hw_a_domain is the hardware observer domain; not interchangeable",
    "batch_time is the dmesg idma_batch_obs part=time record for the trial seq; done_to_read_cycles is that line's done_to_read counter; batch_time.cycles is the same line's hardware cycles (compare with p4m.cycles)",
    "part=time records sharing one seq but differing are kept as batch_time_variants and flagged (part_time_seq_conflict); the first is shown, never a silent overwrite",
    "null means missing capture or mathematically undefined (window <= 0, zero baseline, absent field); only mathematically invalid values are ignored and n_missing counts them",
    "objective stats are descriptive only: no outlier filtering, no significance test, no rerun, no experiment control",
    "records.json is a list of untouched CLI JSON objects (parsed dicts only); captures.json keeps every trial wrapper including partial/failed with raw_stdout and line references",
    "trial count is capped at 60; unrun/uncaptured trials are reported as remaining, never counted as completed"
  ]
